# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the export.
#
# The addresses of the site before the data plane was rewritten, sent to the
# pages that show the same thing now. The old site wrote one page for each
# season, meeting and race it had, at /seasons/<year>/<round>/<type>/, and
# nothing else under those paths. Each of them is listed here, with and
# without its trailing slash, because a rule matches one path exactly. The
# browser keeps a fragment across a redirect, so #lap-times still opens the
# lap times.
#
# No rule has a placeholder. /seasons/ is still a page, and a rule such as
# /seasons/:year would also take the files Next writes beside it, which the
# router fetches to change page (/seasons/index.txt, /seasons/__next._tree.txt).
#
# A race and a meeting are sent by F1's key, which does not move with the
# calendar. The old site numbered 2026 before Bahrain became round 16, so its
# rounds 16 to 22 are today's 17 to 23. Those meetings have no key until one
# of their sessions is published, and are sent by today's round with a 302,
# since a round can move again.

